{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 13, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 13, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=14&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=12&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 746518481, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r746518481-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Jay Shiva", "text": "This place is heaven for me. I would like to recommend all spiritual person to go this place recharge your energy and got blessed from Lord Shiva 🙏", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "25B43824793CD893EA8BE7FFCA31DCCD", "name": "Ryan", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/RyanEverest", "username": "RyanEverest", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 1, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-21", "published_at_date": "2020-02-21"}, {"review_id": 745342297, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r745342297-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "This temple was humbling", "text": "What a privilege to visit here, sharing in the funeral ceremony of the people's loved ones, learning more about their religious beliefs and customs, highly recommend a visit.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5C813146D8AE5D359A8F16E6D639F0A9", "name": "Deanna D", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DeannaD140", "username": "DeannaD140", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/6d/default-avatar-2020-19.jpg", "contribution_count": 29, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255098, "location_name": "Victoria", "location_name_detailed": "Victoria, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-16", "published_at_date": "2020-02-16"}, {"review_id": 745236572, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r745236572-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Worth a see, but Westerners beware before you go.", "text": "The many reviews cover this attraction well. I have been here four times. The largest Hindu temple complex in the world. Worth seeing, but know what you are in for as a Westerner. Be aware and expect the following as part of a unique cultural experience: \n1. Filthy and smelly. Litter everywhere. \n2. Open cremations. Real corpses being burned in open view.\n3. Beggars and solicitors will target you relentlessly. \n4. You will walk through monkey and cow manure.\n5. Watch for monkeys and other pickpockets!\n6. The \"holy men\" are really beggars dressed to earn rupees from tourists.\n7. Open sewage in the river, sometimes with children swimming in it!\n8. Sensory overload, and I mean all five!\n9. The hawkers will try to guess your religion and sell you an appropriate trinket.\n10. You are viewed as a profit opportunity. You will be charged more for everything. Do not be offended. The $11 admission is well worth it.\nWhy would I recommend going? Because you will not see another Hindu temple complex like this one anywhere else in the world. The contrast of filth and beauty is stunning and typifies our human experience.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DA63C0CB65C16BDDBD3BA89AD60EB99C", "name": "mikeej99", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mikeej99", "username": "mikeej99", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f0/9f/default-avatar-2020-16.jpg", "contribution_count": 133, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 33045, "location_name": "Santa Barbara", "location_name_detailed": "Santa Barbara, California"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-15", "published_at_date": "2020-02-15"}, {"review_id": 745179693, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r745179693-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu temples ", "text": "The largest famous Hindu shiva temple  call pashupatinath temple nice organition  very good condition and clean ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "25A76C8CAF835884444765D297A02DCE", "name": "Hariram R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/hariramr2020", "username": "hariramr2020", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f4/d0/default-avatar-2020-33.jpg", "contribution_count": 4, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-15", "published_at_date": "2020-02-15"}, {"review_id": 745098689, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r745098689-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "An amazing, enlightening and sobering experience", "text": "Said by our guide to be the biggest Hindu temple complex in the world it is a collection of quite impressive structures strung along the sides of the Bagmati river. You cannot actually enter the main actual temple unless you are a Hindu but the most dramatic sight is the cremation ghats along the river where the Hindu cremation rituals are practised day and night. Although normal for Hindus the sight of the burning structures smoking along the banks of the river, indeed many people seemed to be treating the site as an afternoon outing, is sobering and thought provoking. Not to forget the gaudily coloured holy men who may relieve you of money to take pictures.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "214EF32618286203F455A70496AC9238", "name": "John B", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/JohnB2151", "username": "JohnB2151", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/03/1e/d1/70/johnb2151.jpg", "contribution_count": 242, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/e5/1c/ae/the-cremation-ghats.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/e5/1c/b4/holy-men.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/e5/1c/c1/general-view-of-some.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2020-02-14", "published_at_date": "2020-02-15"}, {"review_id": 744994300, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r744994300-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Nice", "text": "Pashupatinath temple is known as one of the most powerful temple for hindusum..\nThere were so many peoples out there.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B269EF2E5EAB2617319D5FDABA2E0248", "name": "Sanjog", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Sanjog29", "username": "Sanjog29", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/6d/default-avatar-2020-19.jpg", "contribution_count": 7, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-14", "published_at_date": "2020-02-14"}, {"review_id": 744804389, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r744804389-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Religious ", "text": "This is one of the religious  place of nepal and this place is only for hindu people but other religious people  also can view this place from outside", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 8, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4D5C7CD098BC71755B08B763255CC414", "name": "mrr", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rabindrapoudel", "username": "rabindrapoudel", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/e1/9a/18/avatar.jpg", "contribution_count": 10, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-13", "published_at_date": "2020-02-13"}, {"review_id": 744568277, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r744568277-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Beautiful History!", "text": "Pashupatinath Temple is a beautiful old structure. You can't enter the actual temple if you're not Hindu, however, it is still worth having a wander around the complex and you can see some of the beauty inside.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "FEE624533545E73ADCC3F8C3E724E545", "name": "Lauren K", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/laurenkU26HU", "username": "laurenkU26HU", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/73/77/b7/lauren-k.jpg", "contribution_count": 240, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-12", "published_at_date": "2020-02-12"}, {"review_id": 743484386, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r743484386-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A must visit for the experience", "text": "Pashupatinath is one of the four most important Hindu religious sites in Asia for devotees of Lord Shiva. This is considered a very holy place. I walked in to watch 4 different spots along the river engulfed in fire and releasing smoke. And also that familiar smell of me accidently burning my hair with the hair dryer when I was younger. Then I was told that it's cremation going on. I was told that our body is just a vessel and needs to return to the elements of the universe; earth, fire, water, wind and sky. And that was a spot all of it came together. The Nepalese and Indians believe if one is cremated here, they will not have to suffer with rebirth.\n\nI haven't seen this many dead in one place let alone watch them burn. But there was some kind of peace about this place. This place is definitely not for the faint-hearted.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2A152209EF59000AAD39DB07BC844FA0", "name": "Rajeswary R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rajes_rajaindern", "username": "rajes_rajaindern", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ef/9c/default-avatar-2020-14.jpg", "contribution_count": 33, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-02-07", "published_at_date": "2020-02-07"}, {"review_id": 742932848, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r742932848-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A Most Fascinating Hindu Religious Site", "text": "I felt privileged to visit this fascinating Hindu religious site with its hundred plus temples, hospice, prayer and cremation sites, and more. Visit with a tour guide to get as much information as possible. Not to be missed. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2020-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "F5873E9E36F644DDC9A42E598125D1C8", "name": "Bonnie T", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/BonnieT